     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Hi,</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I&#39;m running Rstudio and shiny server on the same EC2 instance (using <a href=\"http://www.louisaslett.com/RStudio_AMI/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(21,142,194)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.louisaslett.com/RStudio_AMI/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YbcMCvpgbcRANCBWQpXOp\">Louis Aslett&#39;s AMI</a>). ( R3.3.1) (RStudio 0.99.903).</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">It&#39;s my first time setting up the configuration of the shiny server, and I have read through the administrator&#39;s guide. I&#39;m nearly there, just a step missing.</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">At EC2, I set up the following ports:</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">- SShH on port 22;</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">- HTTP on port 80;</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">- Custom TCP at 3838;</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">- Custom TCP at 8787.<br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I created DNS records linking the elastic IP to <a href=\"http://bahrainparks.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bahrainparks.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2x8ZbSbxkpo_UgCdHe7HCs\">bahrainparks.org</a></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">When I reach out to the url:</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><a href=\"http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(21,142,194)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1X2chnMkE-Sl3VnkcSlUtA\">http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder</a>, I get my application up and running just fine. </font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">However, at <a href=\"http://mydomain.com/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(21,142,194)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mydomain.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3J57hcyd5kfQbZat81W3l3\">http://mydomain.com</a>, I get the Rstudio login.</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">What I&#39;m looking for is to have the opposite or at least the first requirement:</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">- get the application at: <a href=\"http://mydomain.com/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(21,142,194)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mydomain.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3J57hcyd5kfQbZat81W3l3\">http://mydomain.com</a> (must!)</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">- and Rstudio at <a href=\"http://mydomain.com/rstudio\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(21,142,194)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mydomain.com/rstudio&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2GIEId-oWg7TxcMfIR4Rla\">http://mydomain.com/rstudio</a> (optional)</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I have tried dozens of edits to shiny-server.conf, but don&#39;t seem to be able to get it right.</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">To be clear, I don&#39;t mind that the application runs on <a href=\"http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(21,142,194);box-sizing:border-box\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1X2chnMkE-Sl3VnkcSlUtA\">http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder</a>, as long as this is called when <a href=\"http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(21,142,194);box-sizing:border-box\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mydomain.com/user/AppFolder&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1X2chnMkE-Sl3VnkcSlUtA\">http://mydomain.com</a> is targeted. I have confirmed with AWS that I cannot use DNS to direct to IP/user/folder.</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">My shiny-server.conf:</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">run_as shiny;</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">server {</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> <span> </span>listen 3838 127.0.0.1;</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> <span> </span>run_as :HOME_USER:;</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> <span> </span>location / {</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   user_dirs;</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> <span> </span>}</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">}</font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></span></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I have tried, for example, adding the following line to location / :</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">    app_dir /home/user/AppFolder;</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Or, adding a virtual host by adding:</span><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   server_name <a href=\"http://mydomain.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mydomain.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391288025000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3JbX34Xy_Dnw1t-2GCcN7I\">mydomain.com</a>;</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">and the following to / location:</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">  site_dir /home/user/AppFolder; </font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I have also tried to send RStudio to another port by adding line:</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">&quot;<code style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">www-port=8787&quot; or (3838) </code>to  <code style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">/etc/rstudio/rserver.conf</code></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">But neither have the desired effect. Actually, the only effect this has is to give 502 Bad Gateway when set up to port 3838, even if I have shiny listen to port 80, so there shouldn&#39;t be an IP/door clash.</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Any hints as to what I&#39;m doing wrong?</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">According to the administrator&#39;s guide, it seems to me that what I need is a virtual host, but then again, I guess I&#39;m not understanding the guide... or I would have made it work by now :)</font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Many thanks</font><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(85,85,85)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Joao</font></p></div>"
